%% Sequence: how the viewer keeps its server alive, AFTER PR #5 step 1
%% (2ddcce6, viewer/app.js). Hand-written.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Tab as Viewer tab
    participant Srv as pr-timeline server
    Tab->>Srv: GET /api/events (openLiveness)
    Srv-->>Tab: retry: 3000, then :ping every 25 s
    loop every 5 min while visible, on refocus, on network return
        Tab->>Srv: GET /api/status (verifyConnection)
        Srv-->>Tab: { app: 'pr-timeline', pid, branch }
        Note over Srv: any request resets lastActivity
        opt heartbeat closed
            Tab->>Srv: GET /api/events (re-open)
        end
    end
    Note over Srv: server retired (idle, or --exit-after)
    Tab->>Srv: GET /api/status
    Srv--xTab: no answer
    Note over Tab: show #conn-banner "Viewer server disconnected"
    Tab->>Srv: retry click → GET /api/status (after relaunch)
    Srv-->>Tab: { app: 'pr-timeline', ... }
    Note over Tab: hide banner, reload the current step
